1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,844
Local Incident Commander is a private,
evidence-first SRE agent built for AMD AI

2
00:00:07,844 --> 00:00:09,654
DevMaster Track 2.

3
00:00:09,654 --> 00:00:12,671
The product is deliberately bounded.

4
00:00:12,671 --> 00:00:19,911
It investigates one incident through a
visible four-step state machine and never

5
00:00:19,911 --> 00:00:22,325
runs infrastructure commands
automatically.

6
00:00:22,325 --> 00:00:30,772
The competition runtime uses Qwen3-8B with
vLLM on a Radeon PRO W7900 and ROCm.

7
00:00:30,772 --> 00:00:39,219
The first half of this video is a live
Radeon session captured today, including

8
00:00:39,219 --> 00:00:44,046
the model endpoint and the full Agent
workflow.

9
00:00:44,046 --> 00:00:51,890
Incident evidence stays on the instance,
and the workflow gate recorded zero remote

10
00:00:51,890 --> 00:00:53,097
core requests.

11
00:00:53,097 --> 00:00:57,321
We begin with a checkout latency incident.

12
00:00:57,321 --> 00:01:03,958
The server creates a four-step plan:
inspect deployments, query metrics, search

13
00:01:03,958 --> 00:01:08,181
logs, and synthesize a cited root cause.

14
00:01:08,181 --> 00:01:13,008
The first native tool call inspects
deployment history.

15
00:01:13,008 --> 00:01:18,439
It finds a canary release immediately
before customer impact.

16
00:01:18,439 --> 00:01:22,663
The server assigns a trusted evidence ID.

17
00:01:22,663 --> 00:01:31,713
The model can choose the current tool and
arguments, but it cannot invent tools or

18
00:01:31,713 --> 00:01:32,317
citations.

19
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:36,540
The second tool queries the golden
signals.

20
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:45,591
p95 latency rises from 420 milliseconds to
4.8 seconds and HTTP 5xx errors reach 18

21
00:01:45,591 --> 00:01:46,194
percent.

22
00:01:46,194 --> 00:01:51,625
Hypotheses update as each result enters
the evidence ledger.

23
00:01:51,625 --> 00:01:55,848
The third tool searches sanitized
application logs.

24
00:01:55,848 --> 00:02:01,279
It finds database connection-pool timeouts
and 137 waiting requests.

25
00:02:01,279 --> 00:02:07,916
The trace records the sanitized arguments,
duration, status, and evidence references.

26
00:02:07,916 --> 00:02:15,156
The fourth step synthesizes the causal
chain: a canary pricing lookup increased

27
00:02:15,156 --> 00:02:19,983
database pressure, pool waiters
accumulated, and checkout latency

28
00:02:19,983 --> 00:02:20,587
followed.

29
00:02:20,587 --> 00:02:27,224
Every claim is linked to evidence already
stored by the server.

30
00:02:27,224 --> 00:02:30,241
The response queue is human-controlled.

31
00:02:30,241 --> 00:02:36,878
We approve a rollback simulation and
reject an unsafe connection-pool increase.

32
00:02:36,878 --> 00:02:40,498
Both decisions are immutable audit events.

33
00:02:40,498 --> 00:02:43,515
No remediation command is executed.

34
00:02:43,515 --> 00:02:47,135
Now we ask a follow-up question.

35
00:02:47,135 --> 00:02:54,979
Session memory answers from the existing
evidence and cites only records in this

36
00:02:54,979 --> 00:02:55,582
investigation.

37
00:02:55,582 --> 00:03:01,616
The session survives a browser reload and
a server restart.

38
00:03:01,616 --> 00:03:05,236
Finally, we stop the local model.

39
00:03:05,236 --> 00:03:10,667
Deterministic fallback continues the
investigation with a visible degraded

40
00:03:10,667 --> 00:03:14,287
state, preserving the evidence already
collected.

41
00:03:14,287 --> 00:03:20,321
Model failure is a recoverable state, not
a lost incident.

42
00:03:20,321 --> 00:03:27,561
For the same model prompt, enforce-eager
vLLM measured 39.35 output tokens per

43
00:03:27,561 --> 00:03:32,388
second versus 15.64 for the default
compiled configuration.

44
00:03:32,388 --> 00:03:39,025
This is model-level Radeon evidence; the
workflow gate separately checks ten

45
00:03:39,025 --> 00:03:41,439
complete, three-tool,
zero-unknown-citation runs.

46
00:03:41,439 --> 00:03:49,283
Local Incident Commander turns native tool
calls into a trusted evidence ledger, a

47
00:03:49,283 --> 00:03:55,920
causal root cause, a human decision, and a
recoverable audit trail.
